{"step_index":461,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:45:32Z","input_tokens":2561,"cache_read_tokens":201132,"output_tokens":1001,"content":"### 🏛️ Squad Conclave: Grok Bot & Quantitative Trading Architecture\n\n**Complexity Score**: `5/5` (Architecture, UI/UX Craft, Quant Strategy Engine, Hard AppSec/Financial Risk Boundaries)  \n**Deliberation Log**: [`~/.gemini/decisions/raw/2026-10-19-trading-bot-architecture.md`](file:///Users/dev/.gemini/decisions/raw/2026-10-19-trading-bot-architecture.md)\n\n---\n\n### 1. What We Agree On\n- **Visual Homage**: 1:1 replica of the Video 1 Grok Bot dark cosmic UI (`#070913`, glowing P&L stats, dynamic stepped canvas curve, live copy-trade feed, bottom trader bench).\n- **Zero Hallucination Math**: Mid-price, bid-ask spread, order-book imbalance, realized volatility, and drawdown calculated strictly in deterministic code.\n- **Dependency Strip**: Remove proprietary sponsored harnesses from the leaked prompt (`agentkit.xyz`, `typesafe.ai`) in favor of native standard-library execution.\n- **Safety Boundaries**: Zero real funds or private keys; strict 15% drawdown circuit breaker and pre-order kill switch.\n\n### 2. The Core Tension (Unsmoothed)\n- **Friction Point**: **Self-Contained Simulation Engine vs. Live Public Crypto API Integration**\n- **Stance A (`Forge` & `Pixel` - Simulation Engine)**: Run an interactive, self-contained tick engine with procedural copy-trading logic. *Gain*: 100% deterministic, zero API rate limits, instantaneous dramatic curve scaling (\\$42 $\\to$ \\$5,739), perfect offline reliability. *Sacrifice*: Synthetic trade stream rather than real DEX transactions.\n- **Stance B (`Blueprint` & `Shield` - Live Market Feeds)**: Ingest live BTC/ETH candle data via free public REST/WebSocket APIs (e.g. Binance/DexScreener). *Gain*: Real market regime data and live price action. *Sacrifice*: Susceptible to network latency, CORS restrictions, rate limits, and disjointed copy-trade timing.\n- **Root Cause**: Showcase fidelity and instant usability versus live data pipeline complexity.\n\n### 3. Recommended Actions\n1. **[Core Scaffold]** — Owner: `Forge` — Finalize Vite + React + Tailwind in [`~/Documents/Antigravity/grok-bot-dashboard`](file:///Users/dev/Documents/Antigravity/grok-bot-dashboard).\n2. **[Pixel Cyber UI]** — Owner: `Pixel` — Implement Grok Bot header, glowing stat cards, monospace terminal copy-feed, and trader bench.\n3. **[Stepped Canvas Graph]** — Owner: `Pixel` & `Forge` — Build dynamic canvas curve with vertical dashed handover flags (`@kai_blitz` $\\to$ `FIRED` $\\to$ `@sol_dumpling`).\n4. **[Dual Simulation Engine]** — Owner: `Blueprint` — Build pluggable engine supporting both *Copy-Trading Mode* (Grok Bot) and *Quant Regime Mode* (Trend/Mean-Reversion with quarter-Kelly sizing).\n5. **[Risk & Verification Gate]** — Owner: `Shield` — Integrate 15% drawdown circuit breaker, manual kill switch, and automated test suite.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Your Decision Point\n> **Which core engine mode should we prioritize for the initial release?**\n\n- **Option A (The Viral \"Grok Bot\" Copy-Trading Experience)**: Focused on the exact Video 1 workflow (interactive \\$42 $\\to$ \\$5,739 climb, automated trader firing on 2 losses, live terminal logs, simulation speed controls).\n- **Option B (The Dual Hybrid Engine)**: Delivers Option A's complete copy-trading experience plus a toggleable \"Quant Mode\" incorporating the leaked prompt's regime detection, order-book imbalance, and quarter-Kelly sizing.\n\nWhich direction would you like to take?"}
